{
  "_comment": [
    "Scenario: UC-01 fatigue/drowsiness with staged recovery options.",
    "",
    "Feature 009 (signal-tier redesign): rewritten from the old",
    "driver_profile/vehicle_profile shape to driver_signal_params +",
    "anomaly_signal_params + run_seed_default (data-model.md §2). The vehicle",
    "behaviour model (steering/pedal/lane/ADAS) is retired; the attention signal",
    "is retired. Drowsiness/fatigue are deterministic Tier-3a signals;",
    "anomaly_rate is the seeded-stochastic Tier-3b signal (the only randomness",
    "in the simulation, seeded by run_seed).",
    "",
    "Recovery options (recovery_model gives each activity's fixed drowsiness/fatigue",
    "recovery, applied once per activity — no short/long rest distinction):",
    "  nap_karaoke        — wakefulness (MOVING) -> nap/sleep 3 ticks -> karaoke 3 ticks",
    "  convenience_stretch — wakefulness (MOVING) -> stretch 2 ticks",
    "  postpone           — postpone=true, no stages (acts as continue driving)",
    "",
    "allowed_actions includes decline in addition to accept_rest/postpone, and",
    "acknowledge — a MONOTONY_PROPOSAL's own options are [acknowledge, decline],",
    "so without it the only response recordable for one was 'decline', the",
    "opposite of what happened when the driver took the content up."
  ],
  "id": "uc01_fatigue_recovery_oshikatsu_v0_1",
  "version": "0.2.0",
